**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/out
**/build
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.git
.github
.vscode
docs
**/*.log
.pnpm-store

# Env files never enter the build context — production config is injected at run
# time via `env_file:` in infra/docker-compose.prod.yml. Without the .env.*
# pattern, `COPY apps/web apps/web` would bake a developer's local
# .env.production into a published image layer.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# One deliberate exception: public, non-secret NEXT_PUBLIC_* defaults that
# `next build` must inline into the client bundle. Keeping this as the single
# source of truth beats duplicating the values as Dockerfile defaults.
!apps/web/.env
